From 6b8dbae5807c2202dd4dbc3c31bcb288f9b6740c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:21:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): amber "stalled" for parked kanban work nothing
 is producing [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backend `kanban_stalled` (parked cards whose agent-owned wait passed 2 h) turns the sidebar's grey `waiting`
card glyph amber (`stalled`), distinct from grey waiting and red needs-you; a human ask still wins and live work
still reads as working. The row's kanban counts gain an amber watch count with a tooltip, in both trailing
branches (card figures/age tail and the one-line default). Session tab accent, ⌘]/⌘[ step model and the
automated-row filter take the new stripe; stripe-transition log lines include kanban_stalled.
i18n: sidebar.row.kanbanStalled (en; overlay-gaps for the locales whose neighbours are untranslated).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
